nearshare (1.0.2-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Ship the Nautilus right-click "Send with NearShare" top-level menu
    item SYSTEM-WIDE, at /usr/share/nautilus-python/extensions/
    nearshare_menu.py (debian/extra/nearshare_menu.py, hardcoded to the
    packaged launcher /usr/bin/nearshare) -- confirmed via `dpkg -L
    python3-nautilus` and its README.Debian to be nautilus-python's
    "all-user plugin directory". `sudo apt install ./nearshare_*.deb` is
    now a true one-step install: the right-click item works for every
    user with no per-user `nearshare install` step.
  * No system-wide Nautilus *script* is shipped: unlike nautilus-python's
    extension search path, Nautilus scripts are loaded only from
    $XDG_DATA_HOME/nautilus/scripts, which is per-user with no
    system-wide equivalent -- confirmed by inspecting the installed
    nautilus/nautilus-data package contents. The extension above is this
    package's only (and sufficient) system-wide integration point;
    `nearshare install` still covers the per-user Scripts submenu entry
    for anyone who wants it too.
  * Promote python3-nautilus from Suggests to Recommends, so a plain
    `apt install`/`apt install ./nearshare_*.deb` pulls it in by default
    and the right-click item is active out of the box. Still non-fatal
    if declined or later removed.
  * Add debian/postinst/debian/postrm: best-effort
    update-desktop-database and gtk-update-icon-cache on
    configure/remove/purge, with a note that each logged-in user should
    log out or run `nautilus -q` once to pick up the new right-click
    item (nothing is killed/restarted on the user's behalf).

 -- Dhiva Labs <dhivakar1010@gmail.com>  Thu, 06 Aug 2026 15:30:00 +0530

